# Force LF for all text files regardless of platform/core.autocrlf.
# Without this, Windows checkouts (including GitHub Actions windows-latest
# runners) materialize CRLF line endings for freshly-checked-out files, which
# then fail `prettier --check .` (Prettier defaults to expecting LF) even
# though the exact same content passed the check before it went through a
# git checkout/merge round-trip.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch line endings.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
